hermes-office local patch — NOT an upstream pull request.

Target: clawmem@0.43.5, applied against the installed npm package root
(/usr/local/lib/node_modules/clawmem), AFTER 036 and 040 (this patch builds on
040's separate query-expansion lane).

Why: query expansion is the one lane that can point at a host which is not
always up (a laptop GPU box). Nothing in the fetch path bounds a connect
attempt: expandQuery only attaches an AbortSignal when the caller passes a
deadline, and the CLI/MCP callers do not. A powered-off endpoint therefore
parks the caller in the kernel SYN retry ladder — measured 132s on Linux with
tcp_syn_retries=6 — before the transport error can trip the stock 60s cooldown.
Every fresh CLI process pays it again.

Two independent bounds, both opt-in and inert unless CLAWMEM_QUERY_URL is set:

1. Pre-flight TCP probe (llm.ts): one net.connect with a hard timer
   (CLAWMEM_QUERY_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS, default 400ms). Failure trips a longer
   cooldown (CLAWMEM_QUERY_COOLDOWN_MS, default 300s) because "host powered
   off" does not clear in 60s, then returns the typed fallback. CLAWMEM_QUERY_PROBE=off
   disables it.
2. Abort fuse (store.ts): a deadline for the lane's fetch
   (CLAWMEM_QUERY_DEADLINE_MS, default 8000, 0 disables). This covers the
   half-dead case the probe cannot see — TCP accepts but HTTP never answers.
   A caller-supplied deadline always wins.

Neither bound applies to the shared default instance, so CLAWMEM_LLM_* keeps
stock behaviour.

Measured against the production expandQuery path (real store, real DB):
  powered off (SYN dropped)  132432ms -> 408ms, then 1ms inside cooldown
  live endpoint              3823/3007ms, 5 real lex/vec/hyde expansions
  half-dead (accept, no reply)  >70s  -> 2000ms at CLAWMEM_QUERY_DEADLINE_MS=2000
  lane unset                 4363/4081ms fallback, identical to stock

